Export line planning layer to SAM Route Exchange compatible CSV file to get your coordinates up in the ship's ECDIS.

For each (selected) line feature, the tool creates a separate RTZ file. Route name and file name will be identical. Route name (and hence also file name) will be taken from the "name" field, if it exists and is filled. Otherwise a generic route name will be used.
The route name will be sanitized (no weird characters).
Waypoints will be created at line feature vertices.
The CSV can be opened in Excel and data can be copied over to the SAM Route Exchange Excel sheet, the columns are compatible. Don't copy the header line!
The tool is fully compatible with the Cruise Tools planning universe. Navigational parameters will be added to the CSV output, if the attributes exist in the corresponding fields. Create the planning file with Cruise Tools to avoid field name issues. The following parameters will be considered:

- Speed in knots: speed_kn
- Turn radius in nm: turn_radius_nm
- Course geometry: geometryType (can be "Great Circle"/"Orthodrome" or "Rhumb Line"/"Loxodrome")
- Cross track distance in nm: xtd_port_nm, xtd_stb_nm (will default to the larger of the two)
- Leg report: notes

Navigational parameters of a line will be identical for all waypoint legs. If you require different navigational parameters for the legs, convert "Planning Lines to Vertices" and change parameters accordingly before using the "Export Points to SAM" tool or manually adjust your values in the SAM Route Exchange Excel sheet.
